Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 11:15:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Async target finding (Leaf, resurrected)

Resurrect Leaf's abandoned async target finding, cross-ported from
MC 1.21.8 to 26.1.2 and reconciled with Purpur's AI-goal edits.

Offloads expensive entity/block target searches off the main thread:
a per-world AsyncGoalExecutor drives a GoalSelector ctx state machine
that prepares searches via a Waker, runs them on the async goal thread,
then validates results on the main thread. Default off: when disabled
the config sub-flags are forced false and every goal/selector path
takes the original synchronous branch (vanilla behavior).

Cross-version adaptations:
- GoalSelector: ctx/poll state machine layered on Paper's profiler
  tick()/tickRunningGoals(); availableGoals dirty tracking
- Mob/LivingEntity/ServerLevel/MinecraftServer/DedicatedServer:
  executor + thread lifecycle, ctx cancel on removal
- target goals (Nearest*, HurtBy, ResetUniversalAnger, DefendVillage,
  NonTame, Healable): getTargetConditions() promoted to protected;
  poll()/findTargetAsync() gated on async.search-entity/alert-other
- MoveToBlockGoal: TypeToCheck enum + async block search gated on
  async.search-block; subclasses (Cat*, Fox, Rabbit, Turtle, Drowned,
  Strider, RemoveBlock) route via typeToCheck()
- Avoid/Follow*/LookAtPlayer/Offer/Tempt/Beg/Panda: async entity search
- Sensing: synchronized when enabled; ChunkEntitySlices: synchronized
  entitiesByClass/Type maps when enabled
- Level.getEntities: relax tick-thread assertion for the goal thread

Notes: package moves (Fox/Rabbit/Turtle->animal/*, Drowned->zombie),
net.minecraft.util.Util, GameRules/tag renames handled. FollowBoatGoal
dropped (removed upstream). Default-off keeps the OFF path identical to
vanilla; the feature itself stays experimental/crash-prone as upstream.

